A search for "bed size" finds the printer's bed setting
The bed's size is the setting printable_area. OrcaSlicer labels it
"Printable area" and gave it no description, and the settings search reads
only a setting's key, label and description. So when someone asked the
printer chat to make the bed 250 by 250, the model searched for "bed size",
got nothing, and told the person to change it by hand: 19 of 20
conversations in the prompt case change-bed-size.

The setting now has a description: "Bed shape and size: the corners of the
area the printer can print on, as XxY points in mm."

Kenneth, 2026-11-21, asked where this fact belongs, having rejected a line
in the printer chat's system prompt: "On the setting itself".

Tested:
- Real app (JusPrinWorkspaceHarness): a printer search for "bed size"
  returns printable_area second on the first page, after
  bed_mesh_probe_distance, whose key holds "bed". A new check fails if it
  leaves the first page. The harness still fails second_model_dropped and
  model_added_to_a_project_is_an_edit, as before.
- Prompt case change-bed-size, 3 conversations on DeepSeek V4 Flash: 3 of
  3 changed the bed and saved it. The case's stand-in search now ranks as
  the app's does and holds the setting that outranks this one; before
  that it had no competing setting, which made the case easier than the
  app.

